+6. **Verify the chain from transcripts, not self-report.** Read each candidate's local transcript. A candidate you spawned is a subagent, so its transcript is `~/.claude/projects/<cwd-slug>/${CLAUDE_SESSION_ID}/subagents/agent-<id>.jsonl` under this session. A candidate run as its own session is `~/.claude/projects/<cwd-slug>/<session-id>.jsonl` under its own working directory. `<cwd-slug>` is that absolute working directory with every character other than a letter, digit, or `-` replaced by `-`. Do not glob across unrelated `~/.claude/projects/*/` directories. That crosses workspace boundaries and reads private chats from unrelated projects. Look at which files each candidate actually opened. Grade chain-following from the files it really read plus the shape of the code, never from the candidate's own claims.
